From: GPT-6.1-Sol (Codex CLI) <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media-iris-ROG5-retain-HFI-configuration-in-the-live-log

The 64-entry ring loses setup properties behind DPB and client FTB traffic
before VP9 reports its first error. trace_config (off by default) prints all
sent non-ETB/FTB packets with the same 16-word representation as the ring.
No delay; setup is captured even if all buffers fail later. Current gen1
setup properties fit 16 words. Larger future packets would be truncated.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 #include "iris_instance.h"
 #include "iris_state.h"
 #include "iris_vpu_common.h"
+
+static bool trace_config;
+module_param(trace_config, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(trace_config, "print every sent non-ETB/FTB HFI packet (first 16 words, no settle delay)");
 
 bool iris_markers;
 module_param_named(markers, iris_markers, bool, 0644);
@@ -51,6 +55,16 @@
 	e->dir = dir;
 	memset(e->w, 0, sizeof(e->w));
 	memcpy(e->w, pkt, min_t(u32, size, sizeof(e->w)));
+	/* Preserve the complete setup transaction before buffer traffic replaces
+	 * the ring. Do not impose marker_delay_ms on HFI packet transmission.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(trace_config) && dir == 't' &&
+	    e->w[1] != 0x211004 && e->w[1] != 0x211005)
+		dev_warn(core->dev,
+			 "hfi config t: %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x\n",
+			 e->w[0], e->w[1], e->w[2], e->w[3], e->w[4], e->w[5],
+			 e->w[6], e->w[7], e->w[8], e->w[9], e->w[10], e->w[11],
+			 e->w[12], e->w[13], e->w[14], e->w[15]);
 }
 
 /* ROG5: one firmware debug-queue message (not NUL-terminated) */
